items.description:
A string is valid when:
- it is non-empty;
- it does not start with the literal prefix log- (case-sensitive);
- any other characters, including line breaks, are allowed.

A file name is valid when:
- it is non-empty;
- it contains no forward slash or backslash;
- it does not end with .png (case-sensitive).

A valid Unix file name is a non-empty string that:
- contains no forward slash;
- is neither . nor ..;
- does not end with .tar.gz, .tgz, .zip, or .Z, ignoring case. The suffix must be at the very end and must include the preceding literal dot; names that merely contain one of those suffixes earlier remain valid.

